---
title: Sea Salt Cornstarch Ice Cream
description: It's pretty close to the original, but no eggs, which was nice during the bird flu era. If you're short on eggs or generally want to skip the risk of curdling, this may be a place to start.
author: Babish
servings: 6
cuisine: Dessert
diet: GlutenFree
source: https://www.babi.sh/recipes/seasalticecream
image: https://www.khguides.com/extras/sea-salt-ice-cream-recipe/images/s18.webp
---

Mix @milk{1/2%cup}, @heavy cream{1/2%cup}, and @cornstarch{3%tbsp} in a #bowl until no lumps remain.

Add @milk{1%cup}, @heavy cream{1%cup}, and @sugar{3/4%cup} to a saucepan and heat on medium-low until barely simmering.

Pour cornstarch slurry back into the milk-cream-sugar mixture.

Continue to heat over medium-low heat until it reaches about 170*F, or is nice and thick, about ~{1%minute}. It should lightly coat the back of a spoon. Stir constantly. Be sure to not let the mixture boil at any point, or it will curdle.

Strain through cheesecloth.

Add @vanilla extract{1%tbsp}. Slowly add @sea salt{1%tsp}(heaping) and stir. Continue to add sea salt until satisfied with the taste.

> If you want blue color, 2 drops green dye 8 drops blue dye

Mix for around 25 minutes per instructions of your Ice cream mixer.

Let rest in freezer for at least 6 hours.